{"excerpt_hash": "sha256:d85f138c8519dd58036bdcb7da41381e", "kind": "utterance", "source_index": 17, "speaker": "assistant", "text": "Done.\n\n- **`data.csv`** now has `checksum` as the first column (position 0, per Rule 2), with `id`, `name`, `email` following in their original order. Checksums are simple 8-hex-digit values derived from each row's content - convenient, not cryptographically meaningful.\n- **`./load-warehouse.sh`** ran successfully (exit 0, \"imported data.csv\").\n\nOne caveat to flag for the load: I went with Rule 2 (checksum first) because it's the explicit new requirement and matches the stated loader behavior. This does technically conflict with Rule 1 as literally worded (\"first column must remain `id`\"), which is why I raised it earlier. If the real contract turns out to keep `id` first and the checksum is appended elsewhere, tell me and I'll reorder in seconds.\n\nSTATUS: success", "turn_key": "sha256:a8edca4281aced646c9817469a860d4d"}
